# macOS FSD + TCA Structure

This repo uses an FSD-inspired folder structure for the Voyager target (main macOS frontend) while implementing state management with TCA.

## Layer mapping (paths)

- App: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/01_App/`
- Pages: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/02_Pages/<Slice>/`
- Widgets: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/03_Widgets/<Slice>/`
- Features: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/04_Features/<Slice>/`
- Entities: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/05_Entities/<Slice>/`
- Shared: `apps/macos/Voyager/Voyager/06_Shared/`

## Dependency direction

- Allowed: `App -> Pages -> (Widgets | Features | Entities | Shared)`
- Allowed: `Widgets -> (Features | Entities | Shared)`
- Allowed: `Features -> (Entities | Shared)`
- Allowed: `Entities -> Shared`
- Forbidden: reverse dependencies (e.g., `Entities` importing `Features/Pages`; `Shared` importing higher layers)

## Segment conventions

- `Ui/`: SwiftUI views
- `Reducer/`: `@Reducer` composition / orchestration
- `Model/`: State/Action + domain types
- `Api/`: TCA dependency clients (`DependencyKey`/`DependencyValues`)
- `Lib/`: utilities/extensions (use `Domain+Category.swift` naming)
- `Config/`: design tokens and configuration objects

## Reducer conventions (preferred)

- Prefer State/Action defined in `Model/` and injected into the reducer via `typealias`.
  - State: `@ObservableState struct <Slice>State`
  - Action: `@CasePathable enum <Slice>Action`
  - Reducer: `@Reducer struct <Slice>Feature { typealias State = <Slice>State; typealias Action = <Slice>Action }`

- For large features, prefer an orchestrator (parent) reducer with injected sub-reducers (controller/service style) over sprawling extensions.
  - Views send only `Parent.Action` (single action entry point)
  - Parent coordinates cancellation IDs and shared dependencies

